WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:01.770
 What I'm going
to do in this class

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:07.175
is use the lessons of history
to apply to your daily life.

00:00:07.175 --> 00:00:08.550
That's what I love
about history.

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:11.010
It can really give you
perspective, solace,

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:11.760
and give you hope.

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:16.770
I will use examples
from the four presidents

00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:17.940
I know the best--

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.850
Abraham Lincoln, Teddy
Roosevelt, Franklin Roosevelt,

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:22.530
and Lyndon Johnson.

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:25.230
Each one of these
presidents was a leader

00:00:25.230 --> 00:00:27.990
during a time of great crisis.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.840
We can learn from their
failures and their ability

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:34.110
to acknowledge those failures
and learn from their mistakes.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:37.955
I'd love to just
transport them into you.

00:00:37.955 --> 00:00:40.080
Think of what you learned
from parents, from people

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:41.160
who have experience.

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:43.930
You're learning from generations
that lived before us.

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:46.240
It makes you feel you're
part of a continuum.

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:49.000
You're not just here alone, so
it makes you a deeper person

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:51.790
and maybe even gives you that
great thing called wisdom.

00:00:55.430 --> 00:00:58.400
I think about Abraham Lincoln,
as he scoured the countryside

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.950
for books and he read everything
he could lay his hands on.

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:03.350
He understood that he
was a work in progress.

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:05.060
Nobody's going to be perfect.

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:07.970
The most important thing
for a leader to develop

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:09.290
is the ability to grow.

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:12.140
All of us in our lives are
going to suffer difficult times,

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:14.180
and the question is,
can you get through it?

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:15.350
Can you grow through it?

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:18.090
Can you learn from it?

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:22.710
I'm Doris Kearns Goodwin,
and this is my MasterClass.

